Crash TWOC: what the MIT licence in LICENSE covers
==================================================

LICENSE (the MIT licence) covers this project's own code in this folder (twoc/), and only that. Its copyright
line is the one place the copyright holder's name is written: the package scripts read it from there.
docs/SHARING.md lists the files file by file. In short:

This project's own code (MIT, LICENSE):
  src/*.c, src/*.cpp, src/*.h, src/crash_twoc.manifest   the port: the bridge, the settings and menu, the setup,
                                                          the audio glue; recomp_manual.c's hand-written
                                                          replacements for some of the game's functions are written
                                                          here, but come from studying its program: they share the
                                                          open question of src/recomp/gen below
  CMakeLists.txt, lift.ps1, analyze.ps1, run_twoc.ps1    the build and the launcher
  tools/ (package, capturekit, diag, *.py, *.cmake)      the build, test and package tools
  apu_dll/ (CMakeLists.txt, xemu_apu_dll.c, xemu_apu_api.h, build.cmd)
                                                          the audio library's build, export and interface (the
                                                          LGPL code it builds stays under the LGPL: below)
  data/disc_usa.tsv                                      the supported disc's file list: names, sizes and SHA-256
                                                          only, no game data
  docs/SHARING.md, this file                             documents
  seed_functions.json                                    addresses of functions in the game's program, for the lift

Not covered by LICENSE (each keeps its own licence and notices, unchanged):
  third_party/imgui     Dear ImGui (MIT, Omar Cornut; its stb files MIT or public domain): third_party/imgui/LICENSE.txt
  third_party/smaa      SMAA (MIT, Jorge Jimenez et al.): third_party/smaa/LICENSE.txt
  third_party/xegtao    XeGTAO (MIT, Intel Corporation): third_party/xegtao/LICENSE.txt. src/ao.c follows XeGTAO's
                        sample shaders and ports its GTAOUpdateConstants to C; it names Intel's copyright where it
                        does, and that part stays under XeGTAO's MIT notice.
  third_party/volk      volk (MIT, Arseny Kapoulkine): third_party/volk/LICENSE.md
  third_party/vulkan    Vulkan-Headers (Apache-2.0 or MIT, The Khronos Group): third_party/vulkan/LICENSE.md
  SDL 3                 fetched by CMake into the build folder (zlib; HIDAPI BSD-style)
  ../xboxrecomp         the toolkit (MIT, its own LICENSE and NOTICE), with its audio code from xemu under the
                        GNU LGPL 2.1 or later (xboxrecomp/NOTICE): built into xemu_apu.dll, not into the exe
                        (apu_dll/; its source zip: tools/package/make_apu_source_package.ps1)
  src/recomp/gen        the recompiled code: C translated by machine (lift.ps1) from the game's own program
                        (default.xbe). The MIT licence is not claimed for it; never committed, never packaged as source.
                        Whether the compiled form may be given to others is an open question (docs/SHARING.md,
                        part 3; a question for a lawyer).
  docs/option_b         a disassembly listing of the Direct3D library inside the game's program: the MIT
                        licence is not claimed for it; never packaged.
  The game              Crash Bandicoot: The Wrath of Cortex and its files belong to their owners. Nothing here
                        includes them or grants any right to them.

THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt (made by tools/package/third_party_licenses.py) has every third-party licence's full text.
This is a description of what the project's owner chose, not legal advice.
